  "generator": "numpy.random.default_rng([20261112, 0, task_index]); task_index 0 reach, 1 reach3d, 2 land. One generator per task, used for nothing else.",
  "sets": "Five complete sets of 10,000 resamples are drawn one after another from the task's generator: all bands; close; middle; wide; middle and wide together. A set is finished before the next begins. The middle-only and wide-only sets are drawn and not used.",
  "calls_within_a_set": "Main reading (per resample): for each resample, first rng.integers(0, 40, size=40) for the blocks, then for each band of the set in the order close, middle, wide one rng.integers(0, 8, size=8) for that band's scenarios.",
  "alternate_calls_within_a_set": "Sensitivity only (set at once): rng.integers(0, 40, size=(10000, 40)) for the blocks of all resamples, then for each band of the set rng.integers(0, 8, size=(10000, 8)).",
  "index_order": "Block index i is block number i. Scenario index j within a band is the j-th smallest seed number of that band.",
  "statistic": "A resample's arm mean is the mean over its 40 drawn blocks and its drawn scenarios (8 per band, so the bands have equal weight). A contrast is the difference of two arm means from the same resample.",
  "pooling": "The pooled contrast of resample r is the mean of the three tasks' contrasts at resample r of their all-band sets. Every task has 960 cells per arm, so this equals the difference of means over the 2,880 cells taken together.",
  "which_set_feeds_which_interval": "Per-task steps and pooled steps: the all-band set. D - A close: the close set. D - A distant: the set of middle and wide together.",
  "percentiles": "numpy.percentile with its default linear interpolation, at 2.5 and 97.5 for the 95% interval and at 5 and 95 for the 90% interval.",
  "exact_comparisons": "Each resample's contrast is kept as a whole-number numerator over a fixed denominator (960 per task, 320 close, 640 distant, 2,880 pooled). The percentiles are taken on the numerators, and the strict comparisons with 0 and with 0.20 are made on numerators (0.20 is 192, 64, 128 and 576 of those denominators), so no rounding of a division can decide a name.",
  "order_of_naming_rules": "First the three names for nothing to compare, tested on the cells. Then, for a pooled step, task-dependence from the three per-task 95% intervals of the all-band set. Then the four-way table, with the larger-than-the-margin label."
